# Paper figures

Use `pipeline/lib/figure_style.py`. Captions carry the narrative.

## Starting point

- No axes titles. No figure `suptitle`.
- Panel letters inside the axes, form `(a)`, never outside and never as `ax.set_title`.
- No white patch behind the letter unless the letter sits on a busy mark (`bbox=True`).
- The northwest letter occupies `LETTER_PAD_NW` in `figure_style.py`. Do not put `$P(\tilde{t})$`, $H_0$ counts, cycle vertices, or $p=$ callouts in that pad. If the corner is already used, pass `loc` or `xy`.
- After a rebuild, check every panel for overlapping annotations before stopping.
- Axis labels 12 pt; tick labels 10 pt; annotations and legends 12 pt.
- Export PDF and PNG at 300 dpi with Type 42 fonts.
- Dense insets may drop a point or two. Do not invent a second house style.

## Colour

Individual `#0072B2`, tactical `#D55E00`, team `#009E73`, text `#222222`. Do not mix the two $H_1$ levels on one diagram.

## Do not

Do not put step names or match titles on the axes. If a schematic needs a short in-panel note beside the letter, pass it to `add_panel_letter(..., note=...)`.
